extends RefCounted

## Shared Medieval rules plus only the selected difficulty's mechanics.
const COMMON: String = "CONTROLS\n• L-click or drag a box to select; click a tile to move or an enemy to focus.\n• R-click drag / Space-drag: pan · Wheel: zoom · A: select all · Esc: pause\n\nCAPTURE & HEAL\n• Seated warriors capture spades and hearts; more allies capture faster.\n• Human capture times: 1/2/3/4/5/6+ seated warriors take 12/9/6/4/2/1 seconds. Other races: 16.7 seconds divided by seated warriors.\n• Partial capture progress stays when you leave. Original bases require their original race to be eliminated. Conquered bases can be recaptured while their current owner lives.\n• Each captured enemy base adds 6 capacity; losing it removes that bonus. Spawn speed stays unchanged. Spawns alternate across owned bases in order.\n• Owned spades speed spawning. Owned hearts and bases heal seated warriors at 1.8 HP/sec.\n• Elves heal at 3.6 HP/sec on owned hearts; base healing is unchanged. Elves must be sitting and unattacked for 3 seconds to heal.\n\nSPAWNING & COMBAT\n• Orcs spawn twice as fast. All races start with 12 capacity.\n• Orcs gain +1 capacity per two owned spades or hearts. Converted orcs are shown as (+N) and do not consume spawn capacity.\n• Melee warriors surround enemies; upgraded humans and elves can attack from farther away.\n• Each additional orc engaged on the same target deals +1 punch damage.\n• Humans: 1st kill +2 max HP; 2nd kill +2 punch; 3rd kill unlocks 3-cell reach; 4th kill unlocks a second target adjacent to the first, within reach.\n• Orc killing blows: 25/50/75/100% conversion chance for 1/2/3/4+ distinct orcs that hit the victim in the last 3 seconds, even above capacity.\n• Elves: +1 max HP per kill or damaging assist within 3 seconds. At 28/32/36 max HP, reach becomes 2/3/4 cells.\n• Demons: +1 punch per kill or damaging assist within 3 seconds. At 8/12/18 punch, movement speed is +20%/+30%/+40%.\n• Assist credit is once per death; HP bonuses do not instantly heal. Bonuses reset on respawn. Eliminate all opponents to win.\n• Automatic attacks stay in the same tile. Damage permits 8 seconds of retaliation, then a return to the designated tile. More hits do not reset the timer.\n• Surrounded returners fight the weakest adjacent enemy until an escape opens. Explicit player and enemy-planner orders can assign new movement or attack commands.\n• Difficulty does not change spawn rates; racial and spade bonuses still apply.\n"
const RULES: Array[String] = [
	"EASY AI\n• Enemy units act individually after the opening idle delay (about 22 seconds), choosing capture, attack or healing orders.\n• No coordinated squads or special retreat cooldowns. Wounded units can seek owned hearts/bases through the individual AI.\n",
	"NORMAL AI\n• Enemy squads coordinate after an opening delay of about 22 seconds. Decisions occur every 2 seconds, with local enemy awareness (16 movement cells).\n• Groups usually contain 2–4 units; five recruits split into groups of 3 and 2. Groups share capture and attack orders.\n• Humans capture and fight together. Orcs focus one enemy; when locally outnumbered, they flee toward an enemy base for up to 10 seconds, once every 30 seconds.\n• Elves retreat below 20% HP toward an owned heart/base and recover to 80%. If threatened, they randomly fight back or relocate. No ten-cell healing limit or timed healing cooldown applies.\n• Demons favour weak nearby victims and compare their group's strength with nearby defenders before attacking.\n",
	"EXPERT AI & BONUSES\n• Enemy AI starts immediately. Decisions occur every second, with local enemy awareness (16 movement cells).\n• Enemy humans fill groups to 4 and choose capture targets within five capture tiles, preferring no enemies. They commit and fight for the chosen tile. Losing half the original mission group gives one 50% retreat chance; a retreat goes to the nearest owned heart/base without a range limit, has a 45-second cooldown and lasts until full HP. All stationary humans, including player units, gain +1 punch on owned spades/hearts/bases.\n• Orcs fill groups to 6 and focus one enemy. Locally outnumbered orcs flee toward an enemy base for up to 10 seconds, once every 30 seconds.\n• Enemy elves gain +2 maximum HP per kill or damaging assist (player elves remain +1). Enemy demons gain +2 punch per kill or damaging assist (player demons remain +1).\n• Elves form groups of up to 4 core units; elves with unlocked range may join full groups. Groups prefer separated destinations.\n• Elf priority: heal → protect wounded allies within 10 movement cells → capture → group attacks.\n• At 20% HP or less, elves may retreat only to an owned heart/base within 10 movement cells. Healing-retreat cooldown: 45 seconds from retreat start. They stay until 100% HP.\n• Demons form groups of up to 4. Priority: heal → defend owned tiles within 10 movement cells → capture → group attacks.\n• At 30% HP or less, demons may retreat only to an owned heart/base within 10 movement cells. Healing-retreat cooldown: 30 seconds from retreat start. They recover to 80% HP.\n• Healing cooldowns prevent starting another retreat, not an ongoing recovery. No nearby healing point means no retreat and no cooldown spent. Distance is Manhattan distance to the nearest cell on the healing tile.\n"
]
const TOOLTIPS: Array[String] = [
	"Easy: individual enemy decisions with an opening delay of about 22 seconds. Automatic attacks hold the same tile; retaliation lasts up to 8 seconds before returning.",
	"Normal: coordinated groups of 2–4, opening delay of about 22 seconds, local awareness, race-specific combat and retreats. Automatic attacks hold the same tile; retaliation lasts up to 8 seconds.",
	"Expert: no opening delay, race-specific group sizes and priorities, nearby healing with cooldowns, and +1 human punch on owned tiles. Local awareness and standard spawn rates. Automatic retaliation lasts up to 8 seconds."
]


static func text(difficulty: int) -> String:
	var selected: int = clampi(difficulty, 0, RULES.size() - 1)
	var shared: String = COMMON
	if selected == ClassicSimulation.Difficulty.EXPERT:
		shared = shared.replace("Elves: +1 max HP per kill or damaging assist within 3 seconds.", "Elves: player units gain +1 max HP and enemy AI units gain +2 max HP per kill or damaging assist within 3 seconds.")
		shared = shared.replace("Demons: +1 punch per kill or damaging assist within 3 seconds.", "Demons: player units gain +1 punch and enemy AI units gain +2 punch per kill or damaging assist within 3 seconds.")
	return RULES[selected] + "\n" + shared


static func tooltip(difficulty: int) -> String:
	return TOOLTIPS[clampi(difficulty, 0, TOOLTIPS.size() - 1)]
